{
 "readings": {
  "T1": "decision at d (every weekly decision, T0 included): basket in force at d = the latest non-skipped basket that has taken effect on or before d (bk.basket_at[decision_idx]); every stock with listed weight > 0 is tagged with tag_lookup.tag(ISIN, d) (as of the decision date itself); n = stocks held, k = stocks whose band's SIGN is BUY at d; state IN iff 5k >= 3n (integers). Weights are RENORMALISED to 1 per basket as in T06 (T06 E5; T10.md 3 step 6)",
  "T2": "events: T0 (free; state of decision 0); a state event on the session after decision j >= 1 if state[j] differs from the state held; a basket event on the first session on or after a non-skipped basket's availableDate (Book.basket_events) if the state of the latest decision made before that session is IN; if it is OUT (and no state event) nothing is traded and the basket in force changes (skipped_baskets.csv). The targets at an event use the basket in force at the trade session (bk.basket_at[session]) and the state of the latest decision made before it; two events on one session are one event",
  "T3": "the three-index switch = the same code with state = all three SIGN BUY; hold the parent = state 1 always; the 100% sleeve = state 0 always (T0 only); the constant mix: f = mean over sessions of (stock value / NAV) of the rule's path at the SAME cost and cash, stocks f x w_i, half of (1-f) in GOLDBEES and half in cash, rebalanced at every event of the rule (T0 free)",
  "T4": "R5 thresholds: state IN iff k/n >= t as exact fractions (k*den >= num*n); R6 weight_fs: IN iff the listed weight of the stocks on is >= 0.60 - 1e-12; t07_rule (descriptive): T07.md 3 steps 4-7 with the copied event builder (per-stock tags read at events only)",
  "T5": "float_fs_LMS / float_fs_SML: production's float formula, sum over the bands present of (count/n) * (1.0 if SIGN is BUY else 0.0), bands added in the order Large, Mid, Small and in the reverse order; float_differs if either >= 0.60 disagrees with the integer state",
  "T6": "R4 tag error: default_rng([10, draw_id, book_no]); for each weekly decision in order, for each held stock in increasing ISIN string order whose tag source is 'rank' or 'nonmember_rank', two uniforms u1,u2; replace the band iff u1 < 0.0793, by the first of the other two bands (order Large, Mid, Small) if u2 < 0.5 else the second; membership and unranked tags are not perturbed; events and NAV are rebuilt from the perturbed states; full window, LBES, 20.8 bps",
  "T7": "bootstrap: n = sessions-1 daily log returns; default_rng([11, resample_id, book_no]); starts = rng.integers(0, n-19, size=ceil(n/20)); blocks of 20 consecutive returns, concatenated and cut to n, the same indices for both series; CAGR = exp(sum log r / (n/252)) - 1; interval = numpy.percentile 2.5 and 97.5 (linear) of 1,000 CAGR differences (rule minus comparator); full window, LBES, 20.8 bps",
  "T8": "R7 stretches: maximal runs of decisions with extra = (rule IN, switch OUT); span from the close of the first decision date to the close of the first decision date after the run (or the window's last session); log returns of the rule and the switch NAVs (20.8 bps, LBES) over the span; 'without the largest' drops the daily log returns of the span's sessions (start+1 .. end) of the stretch with the largest |diff| from both series and recomputes exp(sum/(n/252))-1",
  "T9": "V5 sample seed default_rng([12, book_no]) over the book's full-window decision_stocks rows is drawn by the verifier; the engine reports tag reads = sum of stocks held over the decisions, per book and window",
  "V2": "V2 counts: decisions with a Master label dated after the decision date; tags with a snapshot after the decision date; events whose decision used is not before the trade session (T0 excepted, counted separately); decision trade dates not after their decision",
  "V3": "V3 compares the switch, parent and 100%-sleeve NAVs with T06's strategy, hold_parent and sleeve_only on every shared session to 2026-10-22 at 0, 20.8 and 50 bps (relative difference < 1e-12), the decisions' state on every shared date, and always-in at 0 cost against the published NAV (G0)"
 },
